description: Security policies — auth, tenancy, input, secrets, headers
alwaysApply: false
globs: src/**/*, prisma/**
---

## Authentication & Sessions
- Use Better Auth APIs only — never roll custom auth
- Validate session server-side via `auth.api.getSession({ headers: fromNodeHeaders(req.headers) })` on protected routes
- `requireSession` middleware is mandatory on `/api/v1/*` protected routes — never trust client claims alone
- Session cookies: httpOnly, secure in production, sameSite=lax
- Password min 8 chars; consider increasing to 12 for production policy

## Authorization & Multitenancy
- Every org-scoped DB query MUST include organizationId from verified session — never from client input alone
- Use `requireOrgPermission()` before member/invitation/settings mutations
- Prevent IDOR: verify user is member of org before returning org data
- RBAC checks on server — client UI hiding is not security

## Input & Output
- Validate all inputs with Zod schemas — route handlers, query params, request bodies
- Use Prisma parameterized queries only — no raw SQL string concatenation
- Sanitize user-generated content displayed as HTML (use plain text or DOMPurify if rich text added)
- Error responses must not leak stack traces, SQL, or internal paths in production

## Secrets & Configuration
- Never commit .env, tokens, keys, or credentials
- All secrets via environment variables; validate at startup with `src/env.ts` (Zod)
- Never log session tokens, passwords, reset tokens, or API keys
- Rotate BETTER_AUTH_SECRET on compromise; document in `docs/security-policy.md`

## HTTP & API Security
- Security headers via `helmet()` on all responses
- CORS: explicit `CLIENT_URL` only — no wildcard origins in production
- Rate limit auth endpoints (`/api/auth/*`)
- `TRUST_PROXY=true` in production behind reverse proxy (secure cookies)
- Mount Better Auth **before** `express.json()` — see `express-auth.mdc`

## Dependencies & CI
- Run pnpm audit in make security-audit; block high/critical in CI
- Dependabot enabled (already configured)
- No new dependencies without security review

## Logging & Monitoring
- Log auth failures, permission denials, rate limit hits (no PII in logs)
- Do not log email addresses at info level in production
- Redact `cookie`, `authorization`, `set-cookie` in pino-http logs
